                <pb facs="0530" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg450"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1403.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Jackson’s No. 2061, of the 5th instant,
                    has been received, and his refusal to issue to Gustav Frank Eichborn a passport,
                    under the circumstances set forth in the dispatch, has the Department’s
                    approval.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
